From 4d1791b05176579fe282dd34932c8907ad8045fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:19:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: P2P over WebSocket in the test framework

P2PConnection can reach nodes over P2P WebSocket (/p2p/ws) instead of the
raw P2P protocol, as client (connecting to a node) or server (accepting
a node's connection). test_framework/ws_transport.py does the RFC 6455
opening handshake, without compression, and the framing, including
masking, fragmentation, ping/pong and close; P2PConnection keeps treating
the payload as a byte stream, so existing tests work unchanged.

Selected by test_framework.p2p.P2P_TRANSPORT ("tcp" by default, or the
TEST_P2P_TRANSPORT environment variable). p2p_websocket_framework.py
exercises it against a -publicbind listener.
